.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY2_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json:598:      "raw_output": "{\r\n \"schema\": \"PIPD-TT-REGISTER/1\",\r\n \"scope\": \"round-scoped delta register — NOT merged into .hgk/artifacts/TT_REGISTER.json by this round\",\r\n \"round\": \"POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair\",\r\n \"as_of_candidate\": \"dbe387195d25aca32829f84c051b7bf52b5931eb\",\r\n \"merge_handoff\": \"the operator must fold these rows into .hgk/artifacts/TT_REGISTER.json and regenerate its status_summary via tools/tt_summary_check.py --write; merging was deliberately not done here because that register's projection is asserted by tests/test_tt_summary.py and is outside this round's write scope\",\r\n \"count\": 8,\r\n \"tts\": [\r\n  {\r\n   \"id\": \"TT-S4POST-F02-HARNESS-ENV-DEPENDENCE\",\r\n   \"class\": \"TOOLING\",\r\n   \"owner\": \"PKG-08 packaging / DOC-07 verification\",\r\n   \"affected_edges\": \"post-release verification harness -> unittest discovery\",\r\n   \"first_failing_invariant\": \"full-suite pass is environment-dependent\",\r\n   \"detail\": \"10 test modules require git history or built artefacts (test_publication_projection needs a local frozen ref; test_wheel_distribution needs dist/; test_evidence_manifest, test_tooling_executes and test_atomic_requirements need a real checkout). Exported as a git archive with no .git, the PRE-REPAIR base commit 4445db5a already fails with the same 8 failures + 2 errors, so the profile predates this round and is not a regression. The independent checker could only observe the archive/clone environment because its own read-only rule forbade running in the candidate cwd, so it reported FAIL while the operator's checkout run reported 325 OK at base and 383 OK at the candidate.\",\r\n   \"close_condition\": \"the suite either becomes archive-safe (skip-module guards on the environment-dependent cases with a printed reason) or documents the required environment at the top of tests/; then an archive