t-dependent cases with a printed reason) or documents the required environment at the top of tests/; then an archive run and a checkout run agree\",\r\n   \"evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_F02_RESOLUTION.json\",\r\n   \"status\": \"OPEN\",\r\n   \"severity\": \"NON_BLOCKING\",\r\n   \"origin\": \"INDEPENDENT_VERIFY\",\r\n   \"state_round\": \"POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair\",\r\n   \"status_round\": \"dbe387195d25aca32829f84c051b7bf52b5931eb\",\r\n   \"raw_evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_F02_RESOLUTION.json\",\r\n   \"close_criterion\": \"the suite either becomes archive-safe (skip-module guards on the environment-dependent cases with a printed reason) or documents the required environment at the top of tests/; then an archive run and a checkout run agree\",\r\n   \"closed_requires_fresh_verification\": true\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"id\": \"TT-S4POST-F04-CROSS-RECORD-PERMISSION\",\r\n   \"class\": \"CONTRACT_GAP\",\r\n   \"owner\": \"PKG-01 schemas + PKG-05 ECP/receiver handoff\",\r\n   \"affected_edges\": \"ECP.permission.scope -> PD writable scope -> receiver handoff\",\r\n   \"first_failing_invariant\": \"validate_bundle accepts a self-consistent but rehashed permission expansion\",\r\n   \"detail\": \"An independently re-hashed record whose ECP.permission.scope was widened from src/** to ** still validates PASS with 0 findings, because content_hash proves the record is internally consistent and not that it agrees with the bound PD scope. No executor was invoked and no permission was actually granted; this is a contract-closure gap rather than an exercised escalation.\",\r\n   \"close_condition\": \"validate_bundle emits a SEMANTIC finding when an ECP permission scope is broader than the PD scope it is bound to, with POS/NEG fixtures\",\r\n   \"evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json#F04\",\r\n   \"status\": \"OPEN\",\r\n   \"severity\": \"BLOCKER\",\r\n   \"origin\": \"INDEPENDENT_VERIFY\",\r\n   \"state_round\": \"POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair\",\r\n   \"status_round\": \"dbe387195d25aca32829f84c051b7bf52b5931eb\",\r\n   \"raw_evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json#F04\",\r\n   \"close_criterion\": \"validate_bundle emits a SEMANTIC finding when an ECP permission scope is broader than the PD scope it is bound to, with POS/NEG fixtures\",\r\n   \"closed_requires_fresh_verification\": true\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"id\": \"TT-S4POST-F05-SIDECAR-UNVALIDATED\",\r\n   \"class\": \"CONTRACT_GAP\",\r\n   \"owner\": \"PKG-01 schemas (profile sidecar contract)\",\r\n   \"affected_edges\": \"_profile_meta sidecar -> consumer claim interpretation\",\r\n   \"first_failing_invariant\": \"non-record sidecar values are not validated\",\r\n   \"detail\": \"Injecting LOW_RISK_VERIFIED, independent_acceptance=PASS and allowed_claims=[PRODUCTION_VERIFIED] into PI-PKG._profile_meta validates with 0 findings, because the sidecar is stripped before schema validation by design. The compiled bundle emits NOT_ASSESSED and no LOW_RISK_VERIFIED, so the shipped artefact is correct; the risk is a consumer reading validation PASS as authority for sidecar values.\",\r\n   \"close_condition\": \"either declare a minimal schema for the sidecar or state in the consumer documentation that PASS never authorises sidecar values\",\r\n   \"evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json#F05\",\r\n   \"status\": \"OPEN\",\r\n   \"severity\": \"NON_BLOCKING\",\r\n   \"origin\": \"INDEPENDENT_VERIFY\",\r\n   \"state_round\": \"POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair\",\r\n   \"status_round\": \"dbe387195d25aca32829f84c051b7bf52b5931eb\",\r\n   \"raw_evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json#F05\",\r\n   \"close_criterion\": \"either decla